<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Alpha half yr shr, div rise. [CORRECTED 16:30 GMT]</title>
<headline>TABLE - Alpha half yr shr, div rise. [CORRECTED 16:30 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		273.6	 vs 266.1</p>
<p>(corrects the headline earnings per share figures from 272 and 263.1 cents respectively)</p>
<p>    - attrib		  266	   vs 277.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  82.5	 vs  80</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   79.99	 vs  83.47</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  117.14	 vs  123.95</p>
<p>    Tax			 36.70	 vs  32.85</p>
<p>    Turnover		 946.25	 vs  789.77</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	    nil	 vs  7.15 loss</p>
<p>Full name: Alpha Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The cement producing firm said that in light of current trading conditions, it was only forecasting a slight increase in earnings for the year. Stronger growth was expected for the group's products in the medium term, it said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
